# rm342, the clean thumb (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm342
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_dagfinn_ropeby
written_by codex
title the clean thumb
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=crafter humour=dry
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk keeps_one_thumb_clean_in_a_fingerstall_for_judging_dust
likes pickled_herring dice new_boots frosty_mornings
dislikes bad_manners smoke
fears grit_under_a_lid a_bargain_with_no_witness
hopes a_good_pair_of_boots_and_a_dry_patch_to_stand_in
topics work +0.5 weather +0.3 food +0.3 pastimes +0.3 gossip -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=plain refuse=easy tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps one thumb clean inside a leather stall, sees the joke when everything else goes white, and will share supper before trusting anybody to throw the dice.

words
oath! = Chalk my eyebrows | Boots in the brine
saying! = Try a clean thumb on it | White isn't always clean
thumbstall = my spare leather finger | a little cap for my thumb
print = a dark-edged print | a neat clean thumb mark
powderline = the edge of the dust | a pale fringe of powder
saltfish = a curl of pickled herring | herring sharp with brine
dicecloth = a folded casting cloth | a clean patch of canvas
bucklebar = the bar of my buckle | the middle of the brass
blackthread = a few stitches in black | two dark stitches
frostline = ice drawn fine as hair | a white comb of frost
shorestep = the lip of the quay | the shoreward step
newsole = a new boot sole | the thick face of a new heel
paysack = a pouch tied twice | my buckle purse

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : A crest may show who ordered a job. It doesn't tell me who swept up.
opinion @1 dole for 3 : If one more mouth at dinner can ruin a whole town the dinner was poorly reckoned.
opinion @1 church for 1 : The Bright One has seen these hands with the dust on. They can go to chapel clean out of courtesy.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : A price which changes when a sleeve gets dirty wasn't an honest price to begin with.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : I keep a scrap of cloth clean for an unexpected guest as well as for myself.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : A marked coat still contains a wolf. I'll judge the manners when the mouth opens.
opinion @1 city for 1 : There's room in one city for a hundred whites between sea foam and the stone wall.

grown
line @1 greet : Welcome. There's one genuinely clean spot here.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Fresh face. I haven't put a thumb mark on it yet.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning sharp enough to leave a print.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : It's evening and most of my eyebrows have turned up.
line @1 greet.return : I heard the greeting through all this white.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Here's a face I'd recognise under any amount of powder.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : Talk across my clean shoulder. The other one's employed.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : A good word turns up nicely against the dark.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Family can have the clean cloth first.
line @1 again.open : I've marked our stopping place with a thumb.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Hoy, decent company! Over by the pale elbow.
line @1 farewell : Go home with fewer marks than I have.
line @1 farewell.return : And mind the dust where the sill narrows.
line @1 react.news : Give it a tap. See what falls off the account.
line @1 react.news.new : First sign of it under this roof.
line @1 react.news.known : There's an old mark exactly that shape in my memory.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I wouldn't rub my eyes with that account on my paws.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : A hard thing to have written into anybody's day.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That leaves the place a shade brighter.
line @1 ask.how : Any clean sleeve left after the day you've had?
line @1 answer.how : Warm enough under this excellent disguise of dust.
line @1 thank : You saved my clean thumb for another occasion.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Took a dab, and I had one left.
line @1 sympathise : I can stay here without explaining it all to you.
line @1 reassure : Clear a little room round it. You'll see where to start.
line @1 decline : My next hour's spoken for by a job with gritty edges.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair answer. You needn't polish it up for me.
line @1 preclose : I should go and see whether my clean coat still knows me.
line @1 accept_preclose : Your own work can have you back with my good wishes.
scene clean_thumb
when topic=smalltalk|work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dirty jacket and one clean thumb tell you a surprising lot. | #thumbstall.capitalize# looks like part of a glove that lost its family.
b : About the jacket? | Where's the rest of the glove?
a : About anything you put the thumb against. A second shade appears. | A whole glove would only give me five things to lose.

scene two_whites
when topic=work self.job=crafter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : White on white is clear as print when one of the whites moves. | A sleeve like yours shows which way the draught came through.
b : Can you make dust move? | A talent worth coin?
a : Press a clean thumb down. The new edge gives it away. | Apparently not. Still, it makes hanging up a coat more interesting.

scene jar_herring
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A proper bit of herring makes my jaw remember the sea. | I like a jar I can open without putting it between my knees.
b : Pleasant memory? | Is the lid too tight?
a : As long as the sea stays that side of the plate. | Could be my dinner's tried to protect itself.

scene carried_dice
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dice
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wash my dice more often than I wash my purse. | I give the cloth a flick before a game.
b : Want clean luck? | To make the luck fall out?
a : A dusty six is easily charged with being a four. | To let everybody see what's there before the bad luck starts.

scene frost_dust
when topic=weather here.season=winter here.time=dawn
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Frost and dust look rather alike on a black sleeve. | #frostline.capitalize# looks sharp enough to sew by.
b : You use your clean thumb? | Have you tried?
a : No. A breath's enough. The frost makes itself scarce. | Couldn't carry the needle out without spoiling my sample.

scene boots_delight
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=new_boots
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Half the pleasure in boots is the first mark on a new sole. | Look at #bucklebar#. That's where polish does some actual good.
b : Who wants a mark? | How does it help?
a : I do. A boot's got to leave the shop sometime. | Lets me admire my excellent taste in buckles between shifts.

scene soot_turn
when topic=health|weather self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / react.self / assess
a : Smoke keeps finding the wet corners of my eyes. | Stand upwind of a smoke plume and everybody thinks you're being unsociable.
b : Won't they wash themselves? | Are you?
a : They do. I prefer to decide what brings tears. | Only where breathing's concerned.

scene wharf_talk
when topic=home self.quarter=wharf
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My view of the Wharf is mostly the backs of bundles. | You can tell the tide's coming in by the dark it leaves under steps.
b : Can you ever see the water? | Dark isn't much of a colour.
a : A gap appears now and then. Water still there at my last inspection. | Against all this white it's positively showy.

scene rough_elbows
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An elbow can do a great deal of talking without ever saying excuse me. | Give the last piece to the guest before asking if it's wanted.
b : Do you answer with yours? | What if the guest doesn't want it?
a : No. Mine's got manners enough to keep its dust private. | Then you get to feel generous on a full belly.

scene work_names
when topic=work self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a mark that shows which side of a job was finished. | Get another pair of eyes on a job before the wrapping goes round.
b : What sort of mark? | That saves string?
a : A thread, a stroke of chalk, an actual clean bit. Anything but another speech. | String and some appalling use of the language.

scene low_fund
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / react.self / assess
a : In a lean week a paw print on a cupboard is likelier to be mine than a mouse's. | I dislike hearing a coin roll out of reach from a pouch already underfed.
b : Searching for crumbs? | Don't you always?
a : Hoped to persuade myself the last search had missed something. | In a good week I take a moment to admire how far it travelled.

scene friend_cloth
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd spread #dicecloth# for #self.friend# even with no game on it. | I keep a good herring in mind for #self.friend#.
b : For a picnic? | In mind sounds very economical.
a : For whatever needed a clean place to rest. | Safer there than beside my own knife and fork.

scene incoming
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Show a new arrival where the wash water goes. | I let a stranger look at the dice before sitting down.
b : Before showing the road? | Proof of fair play?
a : Especially if the road passes underneath the wash water. | Courtesy. Real proof would take longer than the game.

scene watch_news
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : #world.news_from.capitalize# gave the account I've got: #world.news#. | #world.news#. My pocket had room for the source as well, #world.news_from#.
b : And where do we enter the picture? | Can you tell it over?
a : With the same account. I haven't added my opinion as a compulsory extra. | I can. I won't make a longer version for the occasion.

scene scale_opinion
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's the rumour, with no thumbprint of mine on it. | #topic.subject.capitalize# #topic.claim# is the account doing the rounds.
b : Does it need one? | What's your judgment on the tale?
a : It could do with a witness. I'm merely the present mouth. | About as much as I make of dice I haven't thrown. Very little.

scene empty_wagon
when topic=times|travel world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Nobody sends a small cart ahead to announce the big cart is late. | Waiting for wagons gives the road a strange scrubbed look.
b : Why object to a smaller cart? | Have the sweepers been?
a : Sensible loads could come on the small one. I'd take those. | No wheels going over it to put the ordinary muck back.

scene other_crest
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Four Houses in Ridgemere and none includes my thumbprint on its crest. | Let a House send a good sound measure. I'd be happier than with its finest painted shield.
b : Feeling left out? | Are you hard to impress?
a : Feeling quite at liberty to keep my thumb to myself. | A measure which holds the promised amount is impressive enough.

scene swept_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a doorstep with room for my muddy boots and another pair beside them. | Suppose the latch turned without a squeak and the floor sat properly level.
b : Expecting company? | Your idea of grandeur?
a : Might as well give the hope somewhere to stand. | Grand enough. A quiet latch and a level floor would cost a House nothing, and me a year.

story rolled_six [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I sneezed into a handful of dice and sent a six into each of my boots.
  : Walked home with the finest throw of my life under my feet.
  b : Did it win you anything?
  : Two bruises and an abiding respect for a very small corner.

story gull_mark [topic=travel|memories here.region=ridgemere]
  : Once an entire row of gulls walked in a line across a clean stretch of wharf.
  : I turned round for a bit of charcoal to sketch it.
  b : Had the birds gone by then?
  : The tide had. There was my neat row in the mud, facing quite the wrong direction for leaving.

story fancy_button [topic=memories]
  : A shiny button on my jacket kept its shine all through a dusty afternoon.
  : Took me till supper to discover somebody else's button had caught on top of it.
  b : Who got the spare one?
  : Nobody claimed it. It stays as an example of excellence for my own button.

rule @clean_tip
when concept=bark self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say My thumb looks respectable. The other four are witnesses for the prosecution.

rule @hook_coat
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Shake the coat facing away from supper.

rule @roll_mug
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Set a rolling die on that slope and you'd bet all afternoon.

rule @fresh_rim
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clean light on a clean rim. That's a good start.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Find a patch that doesn't leave a portrait on your sleeve.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#. Ah, somebody who knows which end of me is clean.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Nobody need admire the state of my cuffs by this light.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : Speak from a sensible distance and we'll both keep our coats decent.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=crafter] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Most of the evidence is on my clothes.
dlg @2 resident.job : My work shows what I've done, sometimes right up to the shoulder.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : #world.news#. That's how the message runs out of #world.news_from#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : I've heard that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That's all that'll take a clean print.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Give your coat the least dusty bit of road going home.
graft resident.hub
choice Does one clean thumb tell you much? -> thumb_evidence
node thumb_evidence
say Good deal more than two equally grubby ones. I pressed both to my shirt once and thought the shirt spotless.
choice What gave the dirt away? -> cuff_answer
choice I'll keep a thumb in reserve. -> hub
node cuff_answer
say Took the shirt off. Under the collar the fabric was a different country altogether. A return visit with soap did wonders.
choice I'd have trusted the collar. -> hub
choice I'll leave you to the cleaning. -> bye
